      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Jewell Building, a 1905 timber-frame structure, now houses the Cambridge Museum and is listed on the National Register of Historic Places, reflecting the town’s historic preservation efforts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cambridge_idaho",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cambridge’s climate is classified as hot-summer Mediterranean continental, featuring hot, dry summers and cold, moist winters that can drop below freezing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
